{
  "_about": "Icon usage registry for pos-module-common-styling. Purpose: prevent icon-choice drift across the DS and any UI generated from it — e.g. a 'delete' action must always use the same glyph everywhere (never trash-can in one place and X in another), a 'mail' concept must always use the same glyph (never envelope in one place and paper-plane in another). This file maps FUNCTION/PURPOSE to the one canonical icon name for that purpose, plus every current known usage site. Audience: both AI (check this file before picking an icon for a new feature) and humans (the /style-guide/foundations/icons page renders this data). How to update: whenever a new icon is added to icon.liquid, or an existing icon is applied to a new purpose, add/update its entry here in the same change — do not let this file drift out of sync with icon.liquid (see RULES.md's 'Component change sync' principle, applied to icons). It is also the source icon.liquid is generated from (`npm run build:icons`).",
  "source": {
    "library": "Tabler Icons",
    "url": "https://tabler.io/icons",
    "license": "MIT",
    "package": "@tabler/icons",
    "note": "icon.liquid is generated from this registry by `npm run build:icons`: each entry's `tabler` names the Tabler icon (outline by default, `tablerStyle: \"filled\"` for the filled set), `extraPaths` adds paths to it, `aliases` are extra names for the same glyph and `inAll` puts it in the `icon: 'all'` group. To add an icon: add an entry here (logical name, purpose, Tabler name), then run `npm run build:icons`. Callers only ever use the logical name.",
    "figma": "The Figma file uses the licensed Streamline set (not publishable); code uses Tabler — an intentional Figma ≠ code difference: same logical names and purposes, different glyph shapes."
  },
